From 0bfd9f63aff3eadda8d570e9b7499914a7eb39d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:37:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] usb: move the USB disk utilities to their own USB Application
 tab (owner request 2026-08-05)

New Reaper_USB.asp carries the disk panel (information, health scan,
format, safely-remove, long-term-store badge) that v2.1.7 had parked on
the Long-Term Storage page when the networkmap side-menu was retired;
it belongs next to the other USB services. Same stock backends
(get_usb_info, start_diskscan/start_diskformat, safely_remove_disk,
disk_fsck.xml) plus the read-only reaper_dev.cgi store_status for the
store badge. First visible tab of the USB Application menu group
(menuTrees/menuTree.js); registered in reaper_inject.c reaper_native[]
(own chrome, no self-bounce). Reaper_Storage.asp keeps only the store
selection; no dict change (tab reuses RDST_43). Mock-validated
(standalone + in-shell tab strip + trimmed storage page).
